1
00:01:51,077 --> 00:01:53,577
What's going on?

2
00:01:54,657 --> 00:01:58,617
Well, uh, I think that bamboo tree was possessed.

3
00:02:04,277 --> 00:02:05,697
This can't be good.

4
00:02:06,297 --> 00:02:09,197
We are the notorious Foxy Pirates!

5
00:02:09,437 --> 00:02:11,417
We want more than just a fight from you.

6
00:02:11,597 --> 00:02:13,177
We want a showdown!

7
00:02:15,557 --> 00:02:18,557
A Davey back with the Foxy Pirates!

8
00:02:21,077 --> 00:02:25,237
I'm in your debt.

9
00:02:25,417 --> 00:02:27,637
Come to my house and let me show you some hospitality.

10
00:02:28,117 --> 00:02:29,617
Awesome! I'm starving!

11
00:02:29,937 --> 00:02:30,617
Me too!

12
00:02:30,937 --> 00:02:33,277
Finally home after all these years.

13
00:02:33,517 --> 00:02:35,797
It's a custom in this village to treat visitors

14
00:02:35,797 --> 00:02:39,077
to extra delicious milk from our extra long farm animals.

15
00:02:39,277 --> 00:02:41,717
Village? I didn't see any village out there.

16
00:02:41,897 --> 00:02:42,937
Or a farmhouse.

17
00:02:46,257 --> 00:02:48,357
Now that you mention it...

18
00:02:48,357 --> 00:02:51,717
The whole village is gone!

19
00:02:51,977 --> 00:02:53,397
All our animals, too!

20
00:02:53,477 --> 00:02:54,617
You're nuts, old man.

21
00:02:54,817 --> 00:02:56,057
I know it's been ten years,

22
00:02:56,157 --> 00:02:57,777
but whole villages don't just disappear.

23
00:02:58,117 --> 00:03:00,057
Yes, but this is a special case.

24
00:03:00,697 --> 00:03:02,057
I'll save the explanation

25
00:03:02,057 --> 00:03:04,177
until after we've had a nice cool drink.

26
00:03:04,817 --> 00:03:07,257
I believe I've had some milk tucked away somewhere.

27
00:03:08,257 --> 00:03:08,657
Hmm.

28
00:03:09,317 --> 00:03:10,597
Did you say milk?

29
00:03:10,597 --> 00:03:13,677
You realize you were stuck on those stilts for ten years, right?

30
00:03:17,897 --> 00:03:20,537
I hope this cheese is to your liking.

31
00:03:20,557 --> 00:03:21,437
You think we're stupid?

32
00:03:21,717 --> 00:03:24,617
You can't pass off your disgusting old milk as cheese!

33
00:03:24,877 --> 00:03:27,197
If you don't want to eat it, I won't force you.

34
00:03:27,397 --> 00:03:29,857
But far be it from me till the cheese go to waste.

35
00:03:29,937 --> 00:03:32,557
Wait, so you're saying it's okay to eat this stuff after all?

36
00:03:32,557 --> 00:03:33,437
Are you out of your mind?

37
00:03:34,357 --> 00:03:35,557
What's the big deal?

38
00:03:35,557 --> 00:03:38,237
Some cheese tastes better once it's finally aged.

39
00:03:38,357 --> 00:03:41,157
Your high-stress lifestyles have made your stomachs weak,

40
00:03:41,237 --> 00:03:43,377
whereas laid-back fellows such as myself

41
00:03:43,377 --> 00:03:44,657
can eat whatever we like.

42
00:03:44,937 --> 00:03:46,977
You kids go on your fancy adventures,

43
00:03:47,137 --> 00:03:49,017
but you're shy when it comes to new food.

44
00:03:51,297 --> 00:03:53,337
Someone call the doctor.

45
00:03:53,597 --> 00:03:55,097
What did you think was going to happen?

46
00:03:55,377 --> 00:03:55,897
Moron!

47
00:03:55,917 --> 00:03:57,197
Doctor, someone's getting a doctor!

48
00:03:57,377 --> 00:03:57,657
Hurry!

49
00:03:57,817 --> 00:03:58,837
Wait, that's me!

50
00:04:00,877 --> 00:04:02,137
It's food poisoning.

51
00:04:02,397 --> 00:04:03,257
Yeah, you think?

52
00:04:03,257 --> 00:04:05,817
You're funny, old man.

53
00:04:07,057 --> 00:04:07,857
You okay?

54
00:04:08,937 --> 00:04:11,637
Yes, excluding the fact that the entire camp

55
00:04:11,637 --> 00:04:13,397
packed up and moved on without me.

56
00:04:13,617 --> 00:04:14,397
I see now.

57
00:04:14,777 --> 00:04:16,637
The village didn't disappear, it moved.

58
00:04:16,817 --> 00:04:18,817
That must mean the people here are nomads.

59
00:04:19,197 --> 00:04:22,517
Indeed, and Long Ring Long Land Island is our home.

60
00:04:23,177 --> 00:04:24,257
You are welcome here.

61
00:04:24,557 --> 00:04:25,497
Oh, thanks.

62
00:04:26,017 --> 00:04:29,197
The island got its name from its ring-like shape.

63
00:04:29,617 --> 00:04:31,497
Although it's technically one big circle,

64
00:04:31,497 --> 00:04:33,857
the tide's divided into ten smaller islands.

65
00:04:34,397 --> 00:04:36,737
You probably wouldn't guess that all of the islands

66
00:04:36,737 --> 00:04:37,877
were actually connected,

67
00:04:38,117 --> 00:04:40,497
but once a year, when the tides are at their lowest,

68
00:04:40,657 --> 00:04:42,717
you can see Long Ring's true form,

69
00:04:42,797 --> 00:04:44,077
if only for a few hours.

70
00:04:44,577 --> 00:04:47,497
We use this time to migrate from one island to the next

71
00:04:47,497 --> 00:04:48,597
every three years,

72
00:04:48,757 --> 00:04:50,557
circling the ring again and again.

73
00:04:50,917 --> 00:04:51,237
Oh.

74
00:04:51,617 --> 00:04:53,137
So everyone moved to the next island

75
00:04:53,137 --> 00:04:54,597
while you were stuck up in the trees.

76
00:04:54,717 --> 00:04:55,457
But rotten luck.

77
00:04:55,457 --> 00:04:57,657
That's a good one.

78
00:04:57,777 --> 00:04:59,357
You're a real rebel, old man.

79
00:04:59,537 --> 00:05:01,557
If they stay on each island for three years,

80
00:05:01,677 --> 00:05:03,757
then subtracting the ten years you spent living

81
00:05:03,757 --> 00:05:05,357
on those stupid bamboo stilts,

82
00:05:05,437 --> 00:05:07,057
it would still take a good 20 years

83
00:05:07,057 --> 00:05:09,177
for them to come back around and meet up with you again.

84
00:05:09,277 --> 00:05:10,977
Assuming you don't eat that cheese of yours

85
00:05:10,977 --> 00:05:12,557
and die of food poisoning, of course.

86
00:05:12,737 --> 00:05:14,097
Well, it's sad but true.

87
00:05:14,097 --> 00:05:15,517
I just wish I had my

88
00:05:15,517 --> 00:05:18,577
to ride again.

89
00:05:19,017 --> 00:05:20,217
Then I could cross an island

90
00:05:20,217 --> 00:05:21,797
every time the tides were low

91
00:05:21,797 --> 00:05:23,237
and catch up to the other villages

92
00:05:23,237 --> 00:05:24,517
in only five years.

93
00:05:26,097 --> 00:05:28,077
That's right.

94
00:05:28,237 --> 00:05:30,237
They're the most graceful and beautiful animals

95
00:05:30,237 --> 00:05:31,257
on the whole island.

96
00:05:31,837 --> 00:05:34,577
Once tame, they can be used to cross the grassy plains

97
00:05:34,577 --> 00:05:35,957
with the greatest of ease.

98
00:05:36,597 --> 00:05:38,157
Without them, it would be impossible

99
00:05:38,157 --> 00:05:39,437
for our people to migrate.

100
00:05:40,437 --> 00:05:42,517
After all, our belongings are far too heavy

101
00:05:42,517 --> 00:05:43,577
to carry on our own.

102
00:05:44,097 --> 00:05:45,857
And even if we were strong enough

103
00:05:45,857 --> 00:05:47,037
to move all our luggage,

104
00:05:47,237 --> 00:05:49,077
the tide would still rise and drown us

105
00:05:49,077 --> 00:05:50,517
before we could make it across.

106
00:05:50,637 --> 00:05:52,437
Wouldn't it be easier to take a boat instead?

107
00:05:52,857 --> 00:05:54,497
Yes, of course, but unfortunately,

108
00:05:54,777 --> 00:05:55,777
we don't know how to sail.

109
00:05:56,117 --> 00:05:57,837
And besides, even if we were able

110
00:05:57,837 --> 00:05:59,497
to charge a log post here,

111
00:05:59,637 --> 00:06:01,737
that doesn't mean it would point to the next island.

112
00:06:02,217 --> 00:06:04,137
The land may be split into ten pieces,

113
00:06:04,297 --> 00:06:05,897
but it's all part of the same place.

114
00:06:06,377 --> 00:06:08,517
Suppose I'll just have to wait 20 years.

115
00:06:09,197 --> 00:06:09,937
You'll be lonely.

116
00:06:10,337 --> 00:06:11,357
That's a long time.

117
00:06:11,357 --> 00:06:14,157
Oh, wait a second.

118
00:06:15,037 --> 00:06:18,237
Is a horse like a horse?

119
00:06:18,737 --> 00:06:20,417
Hey, I almost forgot about that.

120
00:06:20,497 --> 00:06:21,997
We saw a horse on the way here.

121
00:06:22,717 --> 00:06:22,937
Huh?

122
00:06:22,937 --> 00:06:28,477
Oh, my sweet little Shelly,

123
00:06:28,577 --> 00:06:30,257
you waited for me all these years.

124
00:06:30,857 --> 00:06:32,437
You're such a pretty girl.

125
00:06:32,657 --> 00:06:33,257
Look at you.

126
00:06:33,377 --> 00:06:34,077
So cute.

127
00:06:34,217 --> 00:06:35,597
I missed you so much.

128
00:06:35,817 --> 00:06:38,237
You sure grown long since I've been away.

129
00:06:38,497 --> 00:06:40,357
Oh, you make me so proud.

130
00:06:40,817 --> 00:06:41,537
Good girl.

131
00:06:41,857 --> 00:06:42,757
That's a good girl.

132
00:06:43,897 --> 00:06:46,817
I'm so sorry if you were lonely while I was gone.

133
00:06:46,977 --> 00:06:48,117
It's all my fault.

134
00:06:48,117 --> 00:06:50,757
I promise I'll never leave you again.

135
00:06:54,917 --> 00:06:56,117
Don't leave her waiting.

136
00:06:56,257 --> 00:06:57,657
She wants to go for a ride.

137
00:06:57,657 --> 00:07:12,797
What a pow, huh?

138
00:07:13,017 --> 00:07:14,517
Even though everyone else left,

139
00:07:14,617 --> 00:07:16,497
she's still hung around all these years.

140
00:07:16,737 --> 00:07:18,237
That's my kind of horse.

141
00:07:18,737 --> 00:07:21,437
I don't know which one of them is happier right now.

142
00:07:21,437 --> 00:07:29,157
Man, that horse sure is fast, huh?

143
00:07:29,237 --> 00:07:30,397
I want to ride it, too.

144
00:07:30,977 --> 00:07:33,557
I see why that old man likes horses so much.

145
00:07:33,797 --> 00:07:36,217
Now that I'm back, let's cross the sea together

146
00:07:36,217 --> 00:07:38,197
as soon as the tide is low again, okay?

147
00:07:38,977 --> 00:07:40,737
You've waited through rainy days

148
00:07:40,737 --> 00:07:43,177
and you've waited through snowy days as well.

149
00:07:43,417 --> 00:07:45,837
But from now on, we'll have nothing but sunshine.

150
00:07:45,837 --> 00:07:57,357
Shelly, are you sure you won't wait here

151
00:07:57,357 --> 00:07:58,477
for Tonjit all alone?

152
00:07:59,017 --> 00:08:01,097
We're taking all your friends with us.

153
00:08:01,677 --> 00:08:03,537
Please, Tonto, wait, come back!

154
00:08:04,057 --> 00:08:05,557
Please, come with us, Shelly.

155
00:08:05,817 --> 00:08:08,957
We won't return to this island for 27 years.

156
00:08:09,477 --> 00:08:10,397
You're going to be lonely

157
00:08:10,397 --> 00:08:12,077
if you have to stay here all by yourself.

158
00:08:13,297 --> 00:08:15,517
We don't know where Tonjit ran off to.

159
00:08:15,517 --> 00:08:17,037
It's not worth waiting here.

160
00:08:17,117 --> 00:08:18,297
He might be gone for good.

161
00:08:18,497 --> 00:08:19,957
I'm going to stay here, too.

162
00:08:20,217 --> 00:08:21,337
Grandpa's coming back.

163
00:08:21,397 --> 00:08:22,437
I just know it.

164
00:08:23,217 --> 00:08:24,037
Don't be foolish.

165
00:08:24,057 --> 00:08:24,677
Let me down.

166
00:08:24,777 --> 00:08:27,037
I'm not going to leave Shelly and Grandpa all alone.

167
00:08:27,237 --> 00:08:27,637
Stop.

168
00:08:27,777 --> 00:08:28,697
Let me go.

169
00:08:29,117 --> 00:08:30,277
Grandpa's coming back.

170
00:08:30,337 --> 00:08:30,997
I know it.

171
00:08:31,037 --> 00:08:32,377
We have to wait for him.

172
00:08:32,957 --> 00:08:33,977
Good luck, old girl.

173
00:08:34,537 --> 00:08:35,157
Live well.

174
00:08:36,057 --> 00:08:36,577
Shelly!

175
00:08:36,577 --> 00:08:36,817
Shelly!

176
00:08:45,517 --> 00:08:57,137
We have to wait for it.

177
00:08:57,377 --> 00:08:58,497
We have to wait for it.

178
00:08:58,497 --> 00:08:59,057
We have to wait for it.

179
00:08:59,557 --> 00:09:00,297
We have to wait for it.

180
00:09:00,357 --> 00:09:00,937
We have to wait for it.

181
00:09:00,937 --> 00:09:17,057
You know this old man's afraid of heights, don't you?

182
00:09:30,937 --> 00:09:52,057
Oh, no!

183
00:09:52,057 --> 00:09:53,937
Are you okay?

184
00:09:53,937 --> 00:09:58,937
Huh?

185
00:09:58,937 --> 00:10:04,937
Shelly!

186
00:10:04,937 --> 00:10:05,937
What happened?

187
00:10:05,937 --> 00:10:07,937
We heard a gunshot!

188
00:10:14,937 --> 00:10:16,937
Ooh, this head!

189
00:10:16,937 --> 00:10:21,937
Here, I'll get it!

190
00:10:21,937 --> 00:10:24,937
Sorry, suckers, but that horse is mine!

191
00:10:24,937 --> 00:10:25,937
Yeah, you tell them, boss.

192
00:10:25,937 --> 00:10:27,937
Put those losers in their place.

193
00:10:28,937 --> 00:10:34,937
Whoever you are, you'll pay!

194
00:10:34,937 --> 00:10:37,937
Whoever you are, you'll pay!

195
00:10:37,937 --> 00:10:40,937
Whoever you are, you don't know?

196
00:10:40,937 --> 00:10:41,937
My goodness!

197
00:10:41,937 --> 00:10:42,937
How rude!

198
00:10:42,937 --> 00:10:46,937
P-p-p-p-p-p-p-p-p-p-p-p-p-p-p-p.

199
00:10:46,937 --> 00:10:49,937
Don't tell me you've never seen this face before!

200
00:10:49,937 --> 00:10:52,937
The only thing I know about your face is that I'm gonna break it!

201
00:10:52,937 --> 00:10:53,937
He really doesn't know me!

202
00:10:53,937 --> 00:10:55,937
Oh, no, don't get depressed, boss!

203
00:10:55,937 --> 00:10:56,937
He's just saying that!

204
00:10:56,937 --> 00:10:57,937
It's a joke!

205
00:10:57,937 --> 00:10:58,937
Everybody knows who you are!

206
00:10:58,937 --> 00:10:59,937
Everybody knows who you are!

207
00:10:59,937 --> 00:11:02,237
Don't tell me you've never seen this face before!

208
00:11:02,237 --> 00:11:05,937
The only thing I know about your face is that I'm gonna break it!

209
00:11:06,737 --> 00:11:08,537
He really doesn't know me.

210
00:11:08,537 --> 00:11:11,537
Oh, no, don't get depressed, boss. He's just saying that.

211
00:11:11,537 --> 00:11:13,837
It's a joke. Everybody knows who you are.

212
00:11:13,837 --> 00:11:15,837
Like you'd have any reason to know him.

213
00:11:15,837 --> 00:11:17,337
Boo-boo-boo-boo-boo-boo-boo!

214
00:11:17,337 --> 00:11:18,837
You're gonna make him cry, Hamburg!

215
00:11:19,537 --> 00:11:21,537
My name is Foxy.

216
00:11:21,537 --> 00:11:25,137
What's mine is mine, and what's yours is mine too!

217
00:11:25,137 --> 00:11:27,737
Fifi, you should see the looks on your dumb faces!

218
00:11:27,737 --> 00:11:30,737
What kind of pants he gets so marked up over some stupid horse?

219
00:11:30,737 --> 00:11:34,037
If I didn't steal that thing myself, then somebody else would do it!

220
00:11:34,037 --> 00:11:35,037
That's enough!

221
00:11:35,037 --> 00:11:36,937
Come, come!

222
00:11:37,337 --> 00:11:38,937
Hold it, Luffy, not yet!

223
00:11:40,037 --> 00:11:41,837
How'd you know my name was Luffy?

224
00:11:42,437 --> 00:11:45,437
Because unlike some people, we did our homework.

225
00:11:45,437 --> 00:11:48,637
Monkey D. Luffy with a 100 million berry bounty.

226
00:11:48,637 --> 00:11:51,757
Roro Noah Zoro with a 60 million bounty.

227
00:11:51,757 --> 00:11:54,157
A lump of cash like that is nothing to scoff at,

228
00:11:54,157 --> 00:11:56,797
especially considering that you only have seven crew members.

229
00:11:57,437 --> 00:11:59,597
Now, with introductions out of the way,

230
00:11:59,597 --> 00:12:01,117
as captain of the Foxy Pirates,

231
00:12:01,117 --> 00:12:03,597
I challenge you, Straw Hats, to a Daveyback fight!

232
00:12:03,597 --> 00:12:04,877
I don't know what that means,

233
00:12:04,877 --> 00:12:06,797
but if you want to fight, bring it on!

234
00:12:06,797 --> 00:12:08,237
I'm sick of hearing you talk!

235
00:12:09,757 --> 00:12:11,917
Wait, now it all makes sense.

236
00:12:11,917 --> 00:12:13,997
I bet that messed up crew we saw on the way here

237
00:12:13,997 --> 00:12:15,917
got challenged to a Daveyback fight, too!

238
00:12:18,637 --> 00:12:20,077
Which way do we turn?

239
00:12:20,077 --> 00:12:20,637
Those!

240
00:12:20,637 --> 00:12:22,157
Where's the Navigator?

241
00:12:22,157 --> 00:12:23,117
Give orders!

242
00:12:23,117 --> 00:12:24,397
What, Navigator?

243
00:12:24,397 --> 00:12:25,437
Captain!

244
00:12:25,437 --> 00:12:26,237
The captain!

245
00:12:27,517 --> 00:12:28,637
This is bad.

246
00:12:28,637 --> 00:12:29,997
I've got to stop him.

247
00:12:29,997 --> 00:12:30,717
Luffy, no!

248
00:12:31,597 --> 00:12:33,437
We're going to end up losing our crew!

249
00:12:33,437 --> 00:12:35,197
What are you talking about, Usopp?

250
00:12:35,197 --> 00:12:38,317
I know this guy's a jerk, but you can't agree to fight him!

251
00:12:38,317 --> 00:12:39,917
Hoi, hoi, hoi, hoi, hoi!

252
00:12:39,917 --> 00:12:41,197
Fe, fe, fe, fe!

253
00:12:41,197 --> 00:12:42,477
Oh, too bad, kid.

254
00:12:42,477 --> 00:12:43,677
But no take backs!

255
00:12:43,677 --> 00:12:45,277
You already agreed, remember?

256
00:12:45,277 --> 00:12:47,117
Bring it on, I believe you said.

257
00:12:47,117 --> 00:12:48,637
Ain't that right, Porcha?

258
00:12:48,637 --> 00:12:50,957
Oh, that was definitely a bring it on, I heard.

259
00:12:50,957 --> 00:12:53,277
And once you say bring it on, there's no turning back.

260
00:12:53,277 --> 00:12:53,997
That's the rule.

261
00:12:54,957 --> 00:12:56,397
Should've kept your mouth shut.

262
00:12:58,317 --> 00:12:58,957
What's wrong?

263
00:12:58,957 --> 00:13:01,357
Don't tell me you aren't man enough to keep your word.

264
00:13:01,357 --> 00:13:02,317
M2!

265
00:13:02,317 --> 00:13:05,357
You're falling into his trap!

266
00:13:05,357 --> 00:13:06,637
But what about the horse?

267
00:13:06,637 --> 00:13:07,277
Come on!

268
00:13:07,277 --> 00:13:09,037
Shelly, oh.

269
00:13:09,037 --> 00:13:10,637
You landed on your back pretty hard.

270
00:13:10,637 --> 00:13:11,837
Don't push yourself too much.

271
00:13:17,597 --> 00:13:19,277
Both of you step aside.

272
00:13:19,277 --> 00:13:19,997
Are you crazy?

273
00:13:21,997 --> 00:13:24,717
Shelly waited 10 years for me to come back.

274
00:13:24,717 --> 00:13:26,317
I won't let you take her!

275
00:13:26,317 --> 00:13:29,277
I know that you're angry, but those are pirates, old man!

276
00:13:31,757 --> 00:13:33,677
You said the fight's already started?

277
00:13:33,677 --> 00:13:34,397
That's right!

278
00:13:34,397 --> 00:13:38,877
A Davyback fight begins as soon as one captain accepts the challenge from the other captain.

279
00:13:38,877 --> 00:13:39,837
No take backs!

280
00:13:39,837 --> 00:13:43,517
In other words, your captain is fighting our captain whether you like it or not.

281
00:13:43,517 --> 00:13:45,757
All you can do is sit back and deal with it.

282
00:13:45,757 --> 00:13:46,717
I don't get this.

283
00:13:47,277 --> 00:13:49,277
If it's a fight, why do I have to sit and wait?

284
00:13:49,277 --> 00:13:51,037
Let's do this right here, right now.

285
00:13:52,317 --> 00:13:53,757
You don't know anything, do you?

286
00:13:53,757 --> 00:13:54,877
It's not a real fight.

287
00:13:54,877 --> 00:13:57,597
It's more like a sports match between different pirate crews.

288
00:13:58,797 --> 00:13:59,837
Exactly.

289
00:13:59,837 --> 00:14:03,597
Supposedly the game originated in a faraway place called Pirate Island.

290
00:14:03,597 --> 00:14:07,037
As the name implies, it's a sort of secret paradise for pirates.

291
00:14:07,037 --> 00:14:10,397
At any rate, the main purpose of a Davyback fight is to plunder

292
00:14:10,397 --> 00:14:12,637
desirable members from another pirate's crew.

293
00:14:13,197 --> 00:14:15,357
Pirates plundering other pirates?

294
00:14:15,357 --> 00:14:15,677
Yes.

295
00:14:16,237 --> 00:14:19,197
No wonder your puny little crew only has seven members.

296
00:14:19,197 --> 00:14:22,157
A Davyback fight is the best way to pull in some new recruits.

297
00:14:22,157 --> 00:14:24,397
Since you're so clueless, I'll tell you how it works.

298
00:14:24,397 --> 00:14:28,157
After each match, the winner can take any crew member they want from the losing team.

299
00:14:28,157 --> 00:14:33,117
And once that person is chosen, they gotta pledge their undying loyalty to their new captain on the spot.

300
00:14:33,117 --> 00:14:36,797
Both crews take their oath in the name of Davy Jones, the Pirate of the Deep.

301
00:14:37,677 --> 00:14:39,997
So if you lose, you lose a crew member?

302
00:14:40,637 --> 00:14:42,077
Now you're getting it!

303
00:14:42,077 --> 00:14:45,677
Also, if the losing team doesn't have any members worth plundering,

304
00:14:45,677 --> 00:14:50,477
the winning captain can add insult to injury by robbing the ship of its jolly roger.

305
00:14:51,437 --> 00:14:54,957
So you're not just betting your crewmates, but the pride of your ship too.

306
00:14:54,957 --> 00:14:58,637
Winning might make you stronger, but losing can leave you with nothing at all.

307
00:14:59,197 --> 00:15:00,797
Might as well be betting your life.

308
00:15:00,797 --> 00:15:06,557
I see. That explains it. That ship without a captain or a navigator or sail.

309
00:15:06,557 --> 00:15:09,037
They must have lost everything in a Davyback fight.

310
00:15:09,037 --> 00:15:13,517
Oh? So you saw the Fang Frog Pirates, or what's left of them at least?

311
00:15:13,517 --> 00:15:16,717
How about we give you a chance to admire our handiwork in person?

312
00:15:16,717 --> 00:15:20,237
Here! Let's have a round of applause for our brand new recruits!

313
00:15:20,237 --> 00:15:22,717
Long live the Foxy Pirates!

314
00:15:22,717 --> 00:15:25,997
Before I came here, I was the captain of the Fang Frog Pirates!

315
00:15:25,997 --> 00:15:26,957
I was the doctor.

316
00:15:26,957 --> 00:15:28,237
I was the navigator.

317
00:15:28,237 --> 00:15:29,837
And I was the shipwright!

318
00:15:29,837 --> 00:15:32,397
We played five three-coin games and lost them all.

319
00:15:32,397 --> 00:15:35,917
The captain, 13 crew members, and our jolly roger taken away.

320
00:15:36,477 --> 00:15:40,077
With so many people jumping ship, I guess it was more like a merger than anything.

321
00:15:42,877 --> 00:15:47,837
What about your crew, huh? You don't care? Just join a new ship and leave them out to dry?

322
00:15:47,837 --> 00:15:52,237
Yeah, no kidding. Those poor saps got a one-way ticket to a watery grave.

323
00:15:52,237 --> 00:15:55,837
Watery grave? That's their problem. Don't look at me.

324
00:15:55,837 --> 00:15:59,517
You're nothing but scum. We're not playing your stupid game. Got it?

325
00:15:59,517 --> 00:16:01,837
There's no way we'd ever sink to your level.

326
00:16:01,837 --> 00:16:05,197
You can say that all you want, but it ain't the crew's decision to make.

327
00:16:05,197 --> 00:16:09,597
The Davyback fight begins the second one captain agrees to another captain's challenge.

328
00:16:09,597 --> 00:16:12,717
What's the matter? Don't you have faith in your captain?

329
00:16:12,717 --> 00:16:17,037
If you don't agree with the decisions he makes, maybe you're better off joining us after all.

330
00:16:18,877 --> 00:16:20,397
Sorry, Nami, but they're right.

331
00:16:20,397 --> 00:16:21,917
Huh?

332
00:16:21,917 --> 00:16:25,597
All pirates take an unwritten oath to follow their captain to the bitter end.

333
00:16:25,597 --> 00:16:29,357
If we turned our back on this fight now, we'd be sailing away in disgrace.

334
00:16:30,317 --> 00:16:32,717
So? Who cares? That's better than losing.

335
00:16:34,237 --> 00:16:37,197
Maybe for you, but I'd rather die than live in disgrace.

336
00:16:38,397 --> 00:16:39,997
The same goes for me.

337
00:16:39,997 --> 00:16:41,757
Are you kidding? Get over yourself!

338
00:16:43,117 --> 00:16:46,157
You know how men can be. There's no point in arguing with them.

339
00:16:46,157 --> 00:16:49,837
Ugh! I'll stop Luffy by force if I have to!

340
00:16:49,837 --> 00:16:51,917
Don't bother! It's too late.

341
00:16:51,917 --> 00:16:57,117
All that's left now is to sit back and wait for the captains to fire a shot to signal the beginning of the match.

342
00:17:02,077 --> 00:17:03,357
Oh, no way!

343
00:17:03,357 --> 00:17:05,677
Ugh. Guess that settles it.

344
00:17:05,677 --> 00:17:07,357
Well, I'm not complaining.

345
00:17:07,357 --> 00:17:09,517
Should be interesting, at least.

346
00:17:09,517 --> 00:17:12,157
He's agreed to the game!

347
00:17:12,157 --> 00:17:13,837
Yee-haw!

348
00:17:23,037 --> 00:17:25,037
Stupid! Stupid! Stupid!

349
00:17:25,037 --> 00:17:25,917
Stupid!

350
00:17:25,917 --> 00:17:28,717
Why didn't you agree? You could end up losing your crew!

351
00:17:28,717 --> 00:17:29,997
You could lose me!

352
00:17:29,997 --> 00:17:31,757
Yee-haw! I'm gonna win this thing!

353
00:17:32,797 --> 00:17:35,677
Now the Daveyback fight is officially underway!

354
00:17:36,237 --> 00:17:39,117
Good! The sooner I can pound your face in, the better!

355
00:17:40,317 --> 00:17:41,757
I'd like to see you try!

356
00:17:41,757 --> 00:17:44,317
All right! Bring it on, split head!

357
00:17:44,317 --> 00:17:46,157
He doesn't like my haircut!

358
00:17:46,157 --> 00:17:47,517
That's not true!

359
00:17:47,517 --> 00:17:51,277
Hey! Apologize to him! Our boss is sensitive about his looks!

360
00:17:51,277 --> 00:17:54,477
He's sensitive about everything! He's got a heart of glass!

361
00:17:56,317 --> 00:17:58,877
How many times do I have to tell you? Don't laugh!

362
00:17:59,517 --> 00:18:03,917
Luffy, now listen, I'm as angry about the old guy's horse as you are, but this is madness!

363
00:18:04,477 --> 00:18:06,397
Good! Use that anger to thrash him!

364
00:18:06,397 --> 00:18:08,477
What are you doing up? I thought you hurt your back!

365
00:18:08,477 --> 00:18:09,437
Leave it to me!

366
00:18:13,917 --> 00:18:15,757
You don't know what you're getting into.

367
00:18:15,757 --> 00:18:23,117
Sausage on the stick! Get your sausage on the stick!

368
00:18:23,117 --> 00:18:27,597
We got rum, we got cheeseburgers, turkey legs, yakisoba, we got it all!

369
00:18:27,597 --> 00:18:31,917
It's time for the opening ceremonies! Everybody, simmer down, simmer down!

370
00:18:31,917 --> 00:18:32,797
You simmer down!

371
00:18:32,797 --> 00:18:33,677
Shut up!

372
00:18:33,677 --> 00:18:35,517
Come on, let's hear the odds!

373
00:18:35,517 --> 00:18:37,677
All competitors get ready!

374
00:18:37,677 --> 00:18:40,397
Split head may be a jerk, but he sure knows how to party!

375
00:18:40,397 --> 00:18:42,957
And check out all the people he invited! Is that his crew?

376
00:18:42,957 --> 00:18:44,397
Wow, there's so many!

377
00:18:44,397 --> 00:18:47,357
Five jumbo yakisobas, please.

378
00:18:48,397 --> 00:18:49,757
Whose side are you on, huh?

379
00:18:51,277 --> 00:18:53,997
Now, let's calm down, boys! We're about to start!

380
00:18:53,997 --> 00:18:56,317
I love you, Portia! Marry me!

381
00:18:56,317 --> 00:19:00,077
Since our challengers have never played this game before, let's go over the rules, okay?

382
00:19:00,877 --> 00:19:03,997
First of all, whatever you lose in one of the matches, whether it's your crew,

383
00:19:03,997 --> 00:19:09,197
your Jolly Roger, or anything else, the only way you can take it back is with another Davey-backed fight!

384
00:19:09,197 --> 00:19:16,797
Second, any crew member taken by the winner must swear undying loyalty to their new captain on the spot, no exceptions!

385
00:19:16,797 --> 00:19:21,997
Third, if your Jolly Roger is taken, you can't ever fly it again, never ever!

386
00:19:21,997 --> 00:19:24,157
Nami! I got you some cotton candy!

387
00:19:24,157 --> 00:19:27,597
I don't know how everyone can be so calm at a time like this!

388
00:19:29,197 --> 00:19:31,677
That's already settled, so you might as well stop complaining.

389
00:19:31,677 --> 00:19:36,797
Finally, if you happen to break any of these rules, you'll be labeled a disgrace to all pirates and

390
00:19:36,797 --> 00:19:40,157
banished to Davey Jones' locker! So do you swear to uphold them?

391
00:19:40,157 --> 00:19:42,077
I swear! I swear!

392
00:19:48,077 --> 00:19:55,677
All right then, Straw Hat, I'll let you choose your fate! One coin, two coins, three coins, it's all up to you, kid!

393
00:19:55,677 --> 00:19:58,237
That's our boss for you! Always a good sport!

394
00:20:00,237 --> 00:20:01,517
What do the coins do?

395
00:20:01,517 --> 00:20:05,757
Decide the number of gains. The boss is letting you choose how many matches you want to have.

396
00:20:05,757 --> 00:20:09,197
You can quit after one, or you can do as many as three if you're feeling lucky.

397
00:20:10,637 --> 00:20:13,837
Well, the more games we do, the more fun we'll have, right? So let's...

398
00:20:13,837 --> 00:20:14,637
Snoopy!

399
00:20:21,117 --> 00:20:21,597
Got it!

400
00:20:23,197 --> 00:20:24,957
Okay, then I'll take three!

401
00:20:28,397 --> 00:20:32,077
You idiot! Why did you add them? And why did you count an enemy, too?

402
00:20:32,077 --> 00:20:32,957
That was easy.

403
00:20:35,517 --> 00:20:39,677
Then it's settled! Three coins, three games, orthodox rules!

404
00:20:40,157 --> 00:20:42,717
Let Davey Jones be our witness!

405
00:20:49,677 --> 00:20:51,917
Huh? So who's this Davey Jones guy?

406
00:20:52,477 --> 00:20:57,357
A pirate who was cursed by the devil and forced to spend all of eternity at the bottom of the sea.

407
00:20:57,357 --> 00:20:59,597
I've never heard of people living underwater.

408
00:20:59,597 --> 00:21:05,117
Well, that's what the legend says. And all the ships and treasures that sink beneath the waves go to his locker.

409
00:21:05,117 --> 00:21:07,037
Never to be seen by anyone again.

410
00:21:07,677 --> 00:21:09,997
I knew the ocean was scary, but that's crazy!

411
00:21:11,037 --> 00:21:11,597
Yummy!

412
00:21:11,597 --> 00:21:16,397
Davey Jones has been taking his picks from all sorts of pirates for as long as anyone can remember.

413
00:21:16,397 --> 00:21:21,517
That's why we call it a Davey-backed fight in honor of the pirate that may someday claim your crew is his own.

414
00:21:23,357 --> 00:21:25,117
The stage of battle is set, sir!

415
00:21:25,117 --> 00:21:39,917
The beats grieve, but the weapon is myöker.

416
00:21:39,917 --> 00:22:09,897
We'll see you next time.

417
00:23:06,151 --> 00:23:13,151
On the next, One Piece, round one, one lap of the doughnut race, I'm gonna be king of the pirates!

